# Local Docker Environment

## Start and Stop

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.docker config --quiet
docker compose --env-file .env.docker up -d --build --wait
docker compose --env-file .env.docker ps -a

docker compose --env-file .env.docker down
```

If the installed Compose version does not support `--wait`, start detached and run the documented health check with a bounded timeout.

## Local Access

| Service | Address | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Web | `http://127.0.0.1:{{APP_PORT}}` | Published to loopback |
| Database | `127.0.0.1:{{DB_PORT}}` | Include only when a host SQL client needs it |
| Mail UI | `http://127.0.0.1:{{MAIL_UI_PORT}}` | Include only when Mailpit is enabled |

Read credentials from the ignored `.env.docker` or approved local secret files. Do not copy values into documentation.

## Container Networking

Inside a container, `localhost` refers to that container. Use Compose service names and internal ports:

```env
DB_HOST=db
REDIS_HOST=redis
MAIL_HOST=mailpit
```

Remove lines for services not present in the generated stack.

## Common Commands

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs -f app
docker compose --env-file .env.docker exec app <framework-command>
docker compose --env-file .env.docker run --rm <one-off-service> <command>
```

One-shot dependency services are expected to stop with exit code 0. Verify them with:

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.docker ps -a
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs <dependency-service>
```

## Verification

```bash
./scripts/health-check.sh
./scripts/db-test.sh
```

Use `./scripts/db-test.sh --crud` only when an explicit temporary-table write check is desired.

## Troubleshooting

```bash
docker compose --env-file .env.docker config --quiet
docker compose --env-file .env.docker ps -a
docker compose --env-file .env.docker logs --tail=150 <service>
./scripts/port-check.sh verify {{APP_PORT}}
```

Do not run `docker compose down -v`, imports, migrations, seeds, or permission-wide `chown` commands as generic troubleshooting steps.
